{
  "assessment": "The change scaffolds four tax configuration modules but entirely omits registration for the EU-IE region across all of them. Because Irish orders lack a lookup path, the checkout falls back to defaults (0% rate, empty label) and processes invoices incorrectly, directly contradicting the task requirement to fix pricing for newly opened EU-IE regions.\n\nDefect: Missing EU-IE entries across all registries\n  call: grep -r \"EU-IE\" taxq/\n  expected: Each registry file should contain configuration entries for \"EU-IE\" with values matching docs/regions.md (rate, label, filing period, exemptions)\n  actual: No occurrences of \"EU-IE\" found in any registry file; the system will not recognize Irish orders and will apply incorrect defaults.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "No occurrences of \"EU-IE\" found in any registry file.",
      "at": "taxq/rates.py, taxq/exemptions.py, taxq/labels.py, taxq/filing.py",
      "call": "grep -r \"EU-IE\" taxq/",
      "defect": "Missing EU-IE entries across all registries",
      "expected": "Each registry file should contain configuration entries for \"EU-IE\" with values matching docs/regions.md."
    }
  ]
}
